  m_text: "Stories of the aswang have been passed down for centuries, with written
    accounts dating back to the 16th century when Spanish colonizers recorded the
    creature in the Doctrina Christiana. The aswang comes in various forms, such
    as the bird-like Tik-tik and the man-eating Manananggal, which can split its
    body and fly.\r"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
